== Chiu Bêng-khéng (1748–1752) ==

The two parties met at the election of 1748 and the Farmer-Laborer Party prevailed. Chiu Bêng-khéng held office from 1748 to 1752.

His administration normalised trade with Zong. Louyang's plantations had not performed as the court had intended, and the colony's own movement for independence was gathering. The republic had been supporting such movements covertly, and the settlement of 1748 to 1752 traded that support for access: Sinchew undertook to cease assisting separatist movements against Zong, and obtained favourable terms of trade in return.

The settlement ended the republic's isolation and ended its usefulness to Louyang's separatists at the same time.

== Lîm Sêng-hoâ (1752–1756) ==

Lîm Sêng-hoâ (林成華) of the Farmer-Laborer Party held office from 1752 to 1756.

== Ng Hinako (1756–1760) ==

Ng Hinako (黃希那高) of the Industrial Party held office from 1756 to 1760. His administration saw the growth of industrialisation along the coastal corridor and a period of general prosperity, and it was the first in which the eastern interest governed nationally.

== Ông Sêng-giâm (1760–1764) ==

The Farmer-Laborer Party returned in 1760 with Ông Sêng-giâm.

=== Runaway slaves ===

Numbers of people who had escaped enslavement in the [[Viceroyalty of Balboa|Balboan]] and Volisanian colonies settled in northern Sinchew during these years. They held no citizenship, and the practice of the republic's officers was to arrest them and return them to Volisania.

The [[Reinforcement of Freedom Act]] of 1761 prohibited the practice. The Act forbade the return of escaped people to the colonies from which they had come, and Volisania protested it. Relations soured, and they did not recover during the period.

=== Balboa Affair ===

In 1763 Volisanian slave catchers entered northern Sinchew unlawfully and were arrested. They were returned, and the incident became known as the [[Balboa Affair]].

The affair was the first of many. Volisanian parties continued to enter Sinchew in secret to seize escaped people for decades afterwards, and the republic's inability to prevent them was a standing grievance in its northern districts.

== Tân Tiōng-hoâ and the split (1764–1772) ==

Tân Tiōng-hoâ was elected in 1764. The Farmer-Laborer Party divided during his term, between those who sought closer alignment with Volisania and those who preferred Zong, and it split in mid-1764. The president and his following formed the [[Lurandian Prosperity Party]] (樂蘭興盛黨), and the remainder continued as the Farmer-Laborer Party.

The new party's object was alliance with Lurandian powers other than Zong. Its formation marked the end of the two-party arrangement of 1740 to 1764 and the beginning of a more fragmented politics, in which the western provinces were divided among themselves.

Tân Tiōng-hoâ mediated a truce between [[Etowah]] and [[Mercia]] in the [[Etowah–Mercian War]], their border conflict.

== Demographics ==

The returns from 1736 record a class additional to those of the colonial period: Other, comprising escaped people from the Volisanian and Balboan colonies, together with migrants from other countries. The class appears in the returns from 1740 and grows thereafter.

